				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$ I_{k} = \frac{{P_{m} }}{{\upalpha }} $$\end{document}Ik=Pmα

CFI was done right after leaves sampling with an IMAG-K2 Imaging-PAM Fluorometer (M-Series Chlorophyll Fluorescence System, WALZ, Germany). A 0.8 s saturating light pulse (ca. 5000 µmol photons m−2 s−1) was applied to each sample immediately before taking the image. ΦPSII is widely used to assess the level of plant stress in seagrasses 54, as is it highly sensitive to stress. ΦPSII in ambient light conditions was computed from each image by “point measurements”, according to the following equation79 :4\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
